SMP probe: PSCI_AFFINITY_INFO + cache-cleaned/uncached mark readout.

We must distinguish "TZ never started CPU1" from "CPU1 started but our early
marks are hidden by the boot CPU's cached zero lines / it died before C init".
The secondary entry runs with MMU/caches off; the boot CPU clears the mark
words with normal cached stores right before CPU_ON, which can hide them.

  iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
    - new sweet_psci_affinity_info() (PSCI_AFFINITY_INFO 0x84000004, level 0;
      0=ON, 1=OFF, 2=ON_PENDING, negative = error);
    - startCPU(): query affinity BEFORE CPU_ON, immediately after the SMC and
      again before returning, store in sweet_smp_aff_before/after/again and
      print them in the CPU_ON log line;
    - before CPU_ON: push the zeroed mark/stage/vector words to PoC and drop
      the boot CPU's dirty cache lines (dc civac + dsb/isb);
    - new boot arg `sweetmtest=1` (default off): after CPU_ON, poll the
      uncached mark for up to 2 s and print the first nonzero value + elapsed
      ms;
    - startAll() timeout: dc civac the mark lines on the boot CPU, then read
      both the cached copy and an uncached copy through an ml_io_map() alias of
      the marks physical page; the timeout IOLog/panic prints
      `ctx=... aff=before/after/again mark=0x... mark_uncached=0x...
       stage=0x...` (entry is the ml_static_vtop() value, ctx the PSCI
      context id);
    - new globals sweet_smp_aff_before/after/again,
      sweet_smp_mark_cached/uncached, sweet_psci_last_context.
  bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
    - SWEET HALT: summary now carries `aff=b/a/g mark=cached/uncached` (plus
      cpu/target/entry/rc/stage/init/sig), one photo = all the SMP data.

Interpretation (plan):
  * CPU_ON rc=0 + AFFINITY off after + off again -> TZ stub / target encoding;
  * AFFINITY off right after, on later -> core came up late;
  * AFFINITY on + mark_uncached=0 -> core started and died before our first
    store (entry/EL/warm-boot issue);
  * mark_uncached != 0 -> the core ran and our timeout logic was wrong;
  * cached=0 but uncached!=0 -> cache false negative confirmed.

Base = post-0149 CI main (reconstructed from the post-0148 buildtree + 0149
patch because the 0149 run did not exist yet).
